@startuml sequence
' Two pages (newpage), so each one is wide enough for a slide
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "User" as U
participant "Client\n(React web / Flutter)" as C
participant "Express API" as API
database "MongoDB" as DB
participant "Brevo SMTP\n(Nodemailer)" as Mail

title Sign up and verify email (1 of 2)

== Register ==
U -> C : enter name, email, password
C -> API : POST /api/auth/register { firstName, lastName, email, password }
API -> API : validate, bcrypt hash password, create verify token (24 h)
API -> DB : create User { verified: false, verifyToken: hash(token) }
alt email already registered
  DB --> API : duplicate key
  API --> C : 409 { error }
else created
  API -> Mail : send verification email (link: APP_URL/verify?token=...)
  alt email fails
    API -> DB : delete the new user
    API --> C : 503 { error }
  else sent
    API --> C : 201 { message }
    Mail -->> U : "Verify your email"
  end
end

== Verify email ==
U -> C : open /verify?token=...
C -> API : POST /api/auth/verify { token }
API -> DB : findOneAndUpdate(token hash, not expired): verified = true, clear token
alt token matches
  API --> C : 200 { message }
else invalid or expired
  API --> C : 400 { error }
end

newpage Log in and search by ingredients (2 of 2)

== Log in ==
U -> C : enter email, password
C -> API : POST /api/auth/login { email, password }
API -> DB : find user by email
API -> API : bcrypt compare
alt wrong email or password
  API --> C : 401 { error: "Invalid credentials" }
else not verified
  API --> C : 403 { error: "Please verify your email first" }
else OK
  API -> API : sign JWT (HS256, 24 h)
  API --> C : 200 { token, user }
  C -> C : store token
end

== Search recipes by ingredients ==
U -> C : type "eggs, tomato"
C -> API : GET /api/recipes/search?q=eggs,tomato  (Authorization: Bearer <token>)
API -> API : requireAuth: verify JWT, set req.userId
alt missing or bad token
  API --> C : 401 { error }
else valid
  API -> API : split terms, singularize, escape regex
  API -> DB : aggregate: match any term, count matches, sort best first
  DB --> API : page of recipes
  API --> C : 200 { results, page, totalPages }
  C --> U : show recipes, best matches first
end
@enduml
